cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, along with the accompanying article."
title: "SPANA: Saturating Perturbation Analysis of Noncoding Activity"
version: "1.0.0"
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/emmerlab/spana"
abstract: >-
  SPANA is R code for analyzing pooled noncoding CRISPR tiling screens with
  two FACS-sorted populations. Guide-level differential abundance is
  estimated with DESeq2 (SPANA-null), using size factors from an empirically
  defined null set of test guides identified by iterative sigma clipping,
  with one-sided depletion and enrichment tests and Benjamini-Hochberg
  correction. Guide-level effects are then averaged (SPANA-scan) across
  sliding genomic windows, tested against an empirical permutation null, and
  merged into peaks. Spatial clustering of significant guides is assessed
  with a nearest-neighbor permutation test (SPANA-cluster).
keywords:
  - CRISPR screen
  - noncoding
  - DESeq2
  - normalization
  - sliding window
  - permutation test
  - R
